this morning we have breaking news from  the Korean peninsula where South Korea  has scrambled jets in response to a  massive show of force by the north  according to reports North Korean war  planes flew nearly 200 flights near the  border in the last several hours  Elizabeth Palmer is following this from  Tokyo Elizabeth good morning  good morning  the South Korean Joint Chiefs of Staff  said that the North Korean planes were  detected in several areas close to the  Border over a period of about four hours  in the middle of the day  all week South Korea and the U.S have  been conducting their largest ever air  grills yesterday they decided to extend  them a decision North Korea has called a  dangerous and awful mistake the U.S  South Korean Alliance and its formidable  equipment have threatened and angered  North Korea's leader Kim Jong-un this  week he fired off barrages of the kind  of short-range ballistic missiles he's  used in record numbers this year just  last month he observed launches that  state media said simulated attacks on  South Korean targets today he turned air  power such as it is North Korea's Air  Force has hundreds of planes but they  are old mostly outdated Chinese and  Russian models still flying them within  a few miles of the contested border with  South Korea and firing artillery rounds  in the area ratcheted up the already  high tension a few more notches  the extended joint South Korean American  Air drills are now due to end tomorrow  and people in this region hope that will  de-escalate the situation but if the  recent pass is anything to go by it  won't last Nate  Elizabeth Palmer in Tokyo thank you
 

